  "question": {
    "text": "The number of points of discontinuity of the function $f(\\mathrm{x})=\\left[\\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{2}\\right]-[\\sqrt{\\mathrm{x}}], \\mathrm{x} \\in[0,4]$, where $[\\cdot]$ denotes the greatest integer function is ________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Check for $\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right]$ and $[\\sqrt{x}]$ becomes integers.<br/>$\\{0,1, \\sqrt{2}, 2, \\sqrt{6}, \\sqrt{8}, \\sqrt{10}, \\sqrt{12}, \\sqrt{14}, 4\\}$<br/>Continuous at $0^{+}$, continuous at $4^{-}$ $\\left[\\frac{x^2}{2}\\right]=[\\sqrt{x}]$, occurs at $x=\\sqrt{2}$<br/>$\\Rightarrow$ Not continuous",
    "image": null
  },
